      "content": "# Legacy V1 VARIANT compaction fixture\n\n`segment_0.dat` is an immutable segment written by the removed V1 VARIANT\nwriter. It must not be regenerated by the current V2 writer.\n\n- Source revision: `fb0b0c5358e341286c30d7af67a6b996a9d50b1d`\n- Generator path: the source revision's\n  `VariantColumnWriterReaderTest::create_variant_rowset`, invoked by a temporary\n  fixture-generation test with the rows described below\n- SHA-256: `0d437cf92471cbb13ee5ee95298d3879e4abf8b0adb9e68a7d35ad2ec811e041`\n- Rows: 8\n- Tablet column: non-nullable `VARIANT`, unique id 1, maximum 2 materialized\n  subcolumns\n\nThe generator writes the rows through the legacy V1 `RowsetWriter` and then\nopens the resulting segment through `BetaRowset::load_segments`, which verifies\nthe persisted footer and trailer. The same row shape was also checked by the\nsource revision's V1/V2 writer compatibility test to contain both materialized\nand sparse subcolumns and to reconstruct the complete root values. The fixture\nincludes objects, arrays, scalar roots, an empty object, a JSON-null leaf, and a\nroot JSON null.\n\nTo reproduce it, check out the source revision in an isolated worktree, preserve\nthe generator's test directory during teardown, and run the generator through\n`run-be-ut.sh` with the V1 parameter. Verify the SHA-256 before replacing this\nfile.\n"
    },
